   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the town law and the public officers law, in relation to the\nresidency requirement for the court clerk for the town of Sodus, in the county\nof Wayne",
    "basePrintNo": "S7980",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7980-2017",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §23, Town L; amd §3, Pub Off L",
    "lawSection": "Town Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S7980\n\nSPONSOR: HELMING\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend the town law and the public officers\nlaw, in relation to the residency requirement for the court clerk for\nthe town of Sodus, in the county of Wayne\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThis legislation would allow the Town of Sodus to employ a court clerk\nwho resides outside of the Town\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nThis bill amends Section 23 of the Town Law, and Section 3 of the Public\nOfficers Law\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nOne of the Court Clerks of the Town of Sodus is not a resident of such\ntown. This bill would allow the position to be filled by a resident of\nWayne County.\n\nThis legislation was requested by the Sodus Town Board, who stated in a\nresolution dated January 23, 2018, that they do not believe any resident\nof the Town is available to fill this position.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Bill\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATION:\n\nNone\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately\n",
    "multiSponsors": {
